Subject: [PATCH] riscv: spl: materialize alignment before the appended DTB

Upstream-Status: Pending

SPL with a separate BSS locates its appended control DTB through
_image_binary_end. When there are no binman symbols and the preceding
image ends four bytes short of an eight-byte boundary, the alignment-only
.binman_sym_table section can become NOBITS. Its padding is then absent
from the objcopy binary, so the appended DTB precedes _image_binary_end
by four bytes and fdtdec_setup() fails with -ENOENT.

Align the end of the existing linker-list output section instead, so
its padding is included in the binary. The linker-list end markers stay
before the padding and their entry counts are unchanged. Retain the
binman section alignment for images with binman symbols.

diff --git a/arch/riscv/cpu/u-boot-spl.lds b/arch/riscv/cpu/u-boot-spl.lds
--- a/arch/riscv/cpu/u-boot-spl.lds
+++ b/arch/riscv/cpu/u-boot-spl.lds
@@ -35,6 +35,7 @@ SECTIONS
 
 	__u_boot_list : {
 		KEEP(*(SORT(__u_boot_list*)));
+		. = ALIGN(8);
 	} > .spl_mem
 
 	. = ALIGN(4);
